.TITLE "pbpaste"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Prints the current content of the macOS pasteboard (clipboard) to standard output.
This command is useful for retrieving text that has been copied to the
clipboard, allowing it to be piped into other commands or saved to a file.

.DIV "ALIAS"
**paste**

.DIV "TLDR"
**pbpaste**
Prints the content of the clipboard to standard output.
> 

**pbpaste > __file.txt__**
Saves the content of the clipboard to a __file.txt__.
> __file.txt__: The path to the file where the clipboard content will be saved.

**pbpaste | grep "__pattern__"**
Filters the clipboard content using __pattern__.
> __pattern__: The regular expression pattern to search for within the clipboard content.

.DIV "SUMMARY"
`pbpaste` retrieves data from the macOS clipboard. It is commonly used
in conjunction with `pbcopy` to move data between applications or within
the command line.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**mac:pbcopy**

documentation: https://ss64.com/osx/pbpaste.html
